{"book":10,"chapter":10,"context":{"chapter":10,"title":"Insult to David's Envoys","summary":"David sends condolences to the new Ammonite king Hanun, but Hanun's advisers call the envoys spies. Hanun shaves off half their beards and cuts their robes to expose them. War follows, and Joab and David defeat the Ammonites and their hired Syrian allies.","background":"A full beard was a mark of a man's dignity, and exposure was deep disgrace, so the insult shamed David himself. David lets the envoys wait at Jericho until their beards grow back (v. 5). The siege of Rabbah, the Ammonite capital, begun after this war, is the setting for chapter 11.","customs":[{"term":"Stank before David","verses":"10:6","note":"An idiom meaning they had made themselves hateful to David."}],"watchFor":["Kindness is mistaken for spying (vv. 2–3).","Joab's battle charge: 'let us play the men for our people... and the Lord do that which seemeth him good' (v. 12).","The Syrian kings make peace and serve Israel (v. 19)."],"connections":["1 Samuel 11:1","1 Chronicles 19:1-5","Isaiah 20:4","2 Samuel 11:1"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיְהִי","vayhi","H1961","Hc/Vqw3ms","and it was"],["אַחֲרֵי","'acharei-","H310","HAcmpc","after"],["כֵן","khen","H3651","HD","thus"],["וַיָּמָת","vaiyamot","H4191","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he died"],["מֶלֶךְ","melekh","H4428","HNcmsc","[the] king of"],["בְּנֵי","benei","H1121","HNcmpc","[the] people of"],["עַמּוֹן","amon","H5983","HNpm","Ammon"],["וַיִּמְלֹךְ","vaiyimlokh","H4427","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he reigned"],["חָנוּן","chanun","H2586","HNpm","Hanun"],["בְּנוֹ","beno","H1121","HNcmsc/Sp3ms","son his"],["תַּחְתָּיו","tachtav","H8478","HNcmpc/Sp3ms","in place his"]],"x":[[9011001,9011003,4]],"xn":1},"2":{"w":[["וַיֹּאמֶר","vaiyomer","H559","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he said"],["דָּוִד","david","H1732","HNpm","David"],["אֶעֱשֶׂה","'e'eseh-","H6213","HVqi1cs","I will do"],["חֶסֶד","chesed","H2617","HNcmsa","covenant loyalty"],["עִם","'im-","H5973","HR","with"],["חָנוּן","chanun","H2586","HNpm"